  "body": "I got into a strange issue with the arm build of ART (both version 1.25 and 1.26) as it seems to just freeze when converting many photos. \nI was lucky enough to be outside when the polar lights danced 2 days ago and I have around 700+ photos in the processing queue. \nI just edited one, copied the profile and pasted to all the others. After this I selected all of them and put them in the queue.\nNow we get to the freeze part. If I choose to save them as JPEGS in the default location ART saves some and than just freezes. I have to force close it and start again. This happens no matter if I use the local hdd or a smb network drive as source and destination.\nHowever, If I use the SDCARD itself in a card reader, this seems to work just fine.\nI cannot imagine what is wrong as I do not see any errors in the macos system logs or in the samba server/client logs.\n\nI am using macOS Tahoe 26.2 on an M2 MacBook Air.\n",
